        "original_id": "b457065b-1dd1-56e7-8962-161f16c6fbef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mario Lemieux\n- Teams and Organizations: Pittsburgh Penguins, Chicago Blackhawks, NHL\n- Events: 1992 Stanley Cup Finals\n- Music: Comeback Kid (band)\n\nFacts:\n- Mario Lemieux was born on October 5, 1965, and he is a Canadian former professional ice hockey player.\n- In the 1992 Stanley Cup Finals, Mario Lemieux and the Pittsburgh Penguins erased a 4–1 first-game deficit against the Chicago Blackhawks, won that game, swept the series in four games, and secured the franchise’s second consecutive and second overall Stanley Cup.\n- Mario Lemieux is the current owner of the Pittsburgh Penguins team.\n- The band Comeback Kid took its name from a newspaper headline about Mario Lemieux returning to the NHL.",
